{{also|Equip.}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|équiper||to [[supply]], [[fit out]]}}, originally said of a [[ship]], {{der|en|fro|esquiper||to [[embark]]}}; of {{der|en|gem}} origin, most probably from {{der|en|gem-pro|*skipōną||to ship, sail, embark}}; akin to {{cog|got|𐍃𐌺𐌹𐍀||ship}}. Compare with {{cog|goh|scif}}, {{cog|de|Schiff}}, {{cog|is|skip}}, {{cog|ang|scip||ship}}, {{cog|non|skipja||to fit out a ship}}. See {{l|en|ship}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪˈkwɪp/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-equip.wav |Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪp|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|equip}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|++|past_ptc2=equipt|past_ptc2_qual=archaic}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[supply]] with something necessary in order to carry out a specific action or task; to provide with (e.g. weapons, provisions, munitions, rigging)
#* {{quote-journal|en|passage=More than 40,000 would-be migrants to Europe have been intercepted at sea since Italy began paying and '''equipping''' the Libyan coastguard to do so in 2017.|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2020/02/13/have-lost-four-years-life-desperate-migrants-stuck-squalid-libyan/|date=13 February 2020|author=Roland Oliphant|work=The Telegraph|title='I have lost four years of my life': the desperate migrants stuck in squalid Libyan camps}}
#* '''1921''', {{w|Rafael Sabatini}}, ''[[s:In Destiny's Clutch|In Destiny's Clutch]]''
#*:it is no more than proper that you should '''equip''' us with a vessel in which to pursue the journey which you interrupted
#* '''1916''', "[[s:Indicator Tells Pursuing Police Speed of Automobile|Indicator Tells Pursuing Police Speed of Automobile]]" in ''Popular Science Monthly/Volume 88''
#*:A semicircular plate, with the numbers in multiples of five up to thirty miles an hour, is '''equipped''' with a pointer, which indicates accurately the speed of the car.
#* '''1698-1699''', {{w|Edmund Ludlow}}, ''Memoirs''
#*: Gave orders for '''equipping''' a considerable fleet.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[dress up]]; to [[array]]; to [[clothe]].
#* {{RQ:Spectator|I|129|2 July 1711}}
#*: The country are led astray in following the town, and '''equipped''' in a ridiculous habit, when they fancy themselves in the height of the mode.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To prepare (someone) with a skill.
# {{lb|en|transitive|gaming}} To equip oneself with (an item); to bring (equipment) into active use.
#* '''2002''', Prima Temp Authors, ''PlayStation 2: Hot Strategies for Cool Games'' (page 69)
#*: Take it down from a distance with a magic spell, or '''equip''' your sword and attack it at close range.

